{
  "title": "Sharetribe Go \u2014 marketplace (2,444\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Sharetribe Go\nDomain: marketplace | Scale: medium | Stars: 2,444\nProblem: Sharetribe Go is a source-available marketplace platform that enables users to build and launch peer-to-peer and sharing economy marketplaces. It provides a complete solution for creating online marketplaces without requiring extensive coding.\nTarget users: Marketplace entrepreneurs, Platform builders, Small to medium marketplace operators, Developers extending marketplace functionality\nCore features: User authentication and profiles; Listing creation and management; Search and discovery with Sphinx indexing; Payment processing integration; WYSIWYG custom landing page builder; Third-party social login (Facebook); Image upload and S3 storage\nIntegrations: Facebook OAuth, Amazon S3, Sphinx Search Engine, Mercury WYSIWYG Editor, Delayed Job, Stripe or similar payment processors\nTech stack: React, jQuery, JavaScript with Webpack + Ruby on Rails 8.1.2 + MySQL 8.4 + Heroku, Amazon S3, Sphinx Search\nKey libraries: devise, omniauth-facebook, haml, paperclip, react_on_rails, mysql2, passenger, thinking_sphinx, delayed_job, rspec-rails, cucumber-rails, factory_bot\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monolithic Rails application with React frontend integration for dynamic UI components while maintaining server-rendered templates\n- Full-text search implemented via Sphinx rather than database queries, improving marketplace discovery performance\n- Asynchronous job processing with delayed_job for background operations like image processing and notifications\n- Comprehensive test coverage using BDD (Cucumber) and unit testing (RSpec) with factory fixtures and Selenium integration tests",
